  "Test": "",
  "Behaviours": "",
  "Questions": "",
  "Ask while driving and you get one answer — nothing starts running. Anything that follows is read against this session: \"in GT3\" is a class on the grid, \"sector three\" is a sector. Say the engineer's name first if a question is not recognised on its own. Switch one off and its phrases go straight to the chat box like any other words.": "",
  "Fastest lap": "",
  "who has the quickest lap of the session. Name a class to ask about that one instead of your own": "",
  "Fastest sector": "",
  "who holds a sector. Say which sector, and a class if you want one other than yours": "",
  "Your best lap": "",
  "what you have done so far": "",
  "Fuel to finish": "",
  "what to fill the tank to, as a percentage, for a stop on the next lap or however many laps away you say. Needs a lap or two of running first, because the burn rate is measured rather than assumed": "",
  "Tyres": "",
  "how much tread is left, and which corner is worst — the one that decides the stint": "",
  "Damage": "",
  "whether anything is bent, and whether anything has come off": "",
  "Fuel and energy": "",
  "what is left. In a car with an energy allocation that is answered instead of litres, because the energy is what ends the stint": "",
  "Where am I slower": "",
  "the corners you are losing time in, averaged over every lap this session rather than read off one. Name a driver, or say nothing and it is the car ahead in your class": "",
  "Where am I faster": "",
  "the same question from the other end — what you are already doing better, which is what not to change while you work on the rest": "",
  "Who is leading": "",
  "who is winning your class, and by how much. Name a class for a grid running several": "",
  "Who is ahead": "",
  "the next car up the road in your class, and the gap to it — which on an endurance grid is rarely the car you can see in front": "",
  "Follow transcription": "",
  "The engineer isn't running in this mode, so there is nothing to hear.": "",
