  "Pick something other than your sim's output so the beep doesn't end up in the recording. Ctrl-click to pick several and everything plays on all of them.": "",
  "Above 1x is real gain, on top of each feature’s own level. Anything that would clip is turned back down rather than distorted, so the loudest calls stop getting louder before the quiet ones do.": "",
  "Beep on record start and stop": "",
  "Ctrl-click to pick several. Leave the first row selected to use the output device set above.": "",
  "Play test cue": "",
  "Level per device": "",
  "Voice sends the recording you just made to the other SimPitRadio users in your session, who hear it out loud. Nothing is sent unless you hold the trigger key — there is no open microphone, and there is no way to turn one on.": "",
  "Plays on the output device set in the Audio tab.": "",
  "Hearing only the cars near you on track is a per-sim setting, because it depends on where everyone is and only the sim knows that. It is in Profiles, under the game's plugin settings, next to \"Recognise standings positions\".": "",
  "Everyone shares one host by default. Creating your own puts the audio on a machine you pay for, near you — SimPitRadio opens DigitalOcean in your browser, and the relay builds it for you. Your cloud account is never handed to this application.": "",
  "Stop powers your host down but keeps it, so its disk is still billed. Destroy is the one that ends billing, and cannot be undone. Reset repairs the configuration without changing the address anyone is connected to.": "",
  "Destroy {name}?\n\nThis cannot be undone. It ends the billing for it; Stop only powers it off.": "",
  "no answer from DigitalOcean — press Create to try again": "",
