  "  ← recommended": "",
  "Region": "",
  "Speaks on the output device set in the Audio tab.": "",
  "These run whenever the engineer does. Repeat is how many seconds before it says the same thing again while it is still true — 0 says it once. A car alongside is worth repeating; a lap time is not.": "",
  "Copy": "",
  "Re-send": "",
  "Say \"focus on P3\" to pick somebody else, \"default focus\" to go back to the car ahead, or \"stop focusing\" for nobody. \"Study Estre\" keeps watching one driver whatever the order does. The Status tab lists whoever is being studied, so a driver who has lost track can look rather than ask out loud.": "",
  "Once a few laps have been driven the circuit's own shape is known, and the lap is cut into corners and the straights between them. Both are always worked out — that is what stops a corner going missing because you are flat through it — but these choose which get shown and compared.": "",
  "The coach's own calls. Separate from the engineer's Behaviours, because turning the coaching down should not turn the spotter down with it. All three still need Coach mode running — none of them says anything until you ask to be coached.": "",
  "Sounds a note every time a tyre reaches the edge of its grip under braking, so you can hear the release rather than guess at it. Done well it comes out as a short descending run; too few notes means the brake was dumped, none at all means the limit was never found, and a low note outside the scale means a tyre locked. You can also start it mid-session by asking for it — \"let's start training on the brakes\".": "",
  "Ask to be shown a corner and the two lines through it are drawn over the game: yours orange through red, theirs indigo through cyan. The shade says what the feet were doing — palest on the brakes, darkest on the power — and both lines are dashed out of step with each other so neither hides the other where they coincide. It only draws over a game running borderless or windowed — nothing draws over exclusive fullscreen.": "",
